5. AIR JUMPS MUST PRESERVE HORIZONTAL MOMENTUM

Audit the current airJump() behavior.

An air jump should primarily add/reset vertical jump velocity.

It should not arbitrarily replace a player’s horizontal velocity simply because Jump was pressed.

If the player is moving quickly to the right and air-jumps, they should continue carrying that horizontal momentum.

If they begin steering left, normal air-control rules should bend/reverse the velocity progressively rather than teleporting the velocity from one direction to another.

The expected flow is:

fast run
→ jump
→ air attack
→ air jump
→ air attack
→ air dash

without arbitrary horizontal speed loss at the transitions.

