13. INPUT BUFFERING

Alva already has a combat attack buffer.

Preserve it and improve its consistency.

The player should be able to press the next intended action very slightly before the current state allows it and have the game perform that action immediately when legal.

Audit buffering for:

* attack after attack;
* attack after landing;
* attack after Dash;
* jump after attack;
* Dash after attack;
* air dash after attack where cancel rules permit it;
* jump immediately before landing.

Do not create enormous buffers that cause old inputs to execute unexpectedly.

The current ~0.15-second combat buffer is within a useful range; tune globally if necessary rather than giving different characters different forgiveness.

