15. HITSTOP MUST ADD IMPACT WITHOUT MAKING THE GAME SLUGGISH

Keep hitstop.

The game still needs impact.

But audit every hitstop value.

Light attacks should have short, crisp hitstop.

Heavy attacks can have more.

A dramatic finishing launch may have more presentation.

Avoid excessive freezes on ordinary rapid combat.

Most importantly, hitstop must temporarily freeze motion, not erase it.

When hitstop ends, stored velocities must continue correctly.

A fighter moving quickly before hitstop should not mysteriously resume slowly afterward.

